# Hide Text checkbox (empty container mechanism)

Adds a **"Hide Text"** checkbox to the shell top bar, immediately **beside the
`#shell-lecture` button**, wired to an initially **empty registry**. Checking the box
applies the class `hide-text` to the `#shell` root and exposes a global `HT()` guard —
but since no element is registered yet, **checking it changes nothing visually**.
Text items get registered later, one prompt at a time, per the v2 "Simplify display"
requests. Registered items are *hidden, never deleted* — user-facing builds get them
back by unchecking (or removing the auto-lecture default).

## Naming tokens (fixed — automation greps for these)

| Token | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `#ht-ctl` / `#ht-toggle` | the label / checkbox in the top bar |
| `hide-text` | class toggled on `#shell` when checked |
| `.ht-hide` | class that registered **DOM** text nodes receive |
| `HT()` | global guard for registered **canvas** text draw calls |
| `HIDE-TEXT REGISTRY` | manifest comment listing everything registered |

## Insertion 1 — markup (in the top bar)

Find the lecture button (present in every CM sim; the v2 particle-physics sims got
theirs from `add-guided-inquiry-and-lecture-mode`):

```html
<button id="shell-lecture" class="shell-btn" title="...">🎓 Lecture</button>
```

Insert **immediately after** its closing `</button>`:

```html
<label id="ht-ctl" class="shell-btn" title="Hide Text — hides registered labels/readouts; registry is empty until items are added">
  <input type="checkbox" id="ht-toggle"> Hide Text
</label>
```

## Insertion 2 — CSS (append inside the sim's main `<style>` block)

```css
/* Hide Text toggle */
#ht-ctl{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;cursor:pointer;user-select:none;}
#ht-ctl input{accent-color:var(--accent);margin:0;cursor:pointer;}
#shell.hide-text .ht-hide{display:none !important;}
```

(If the sim has no `--accent` variable, omit `accent-color`.)

## Insertion 3 — registry comment + wiring script

Place this block **immediately after the closing `</header>`** of the top bar, so
`window.HT` is defined *before* the main sim IIFE runs and plain `HT()` calls are safe
inside draw code:

```html
<!-- HIDE-TEXT REGISTRY ("Simplify display" v2)
     DOM items:    add class "ht-hide" to the element.
     Canvas items: wrap the draw call in  if(!HT()){ ... }
     Keep this list current when registering items:
     (empty — nothing registered yet)
-->
<script>
/* Hide Text toggle — empty registry; hides .ht-hide DOM nodes and gates HT() canvas labels. */
(function(){
  var shell=document.getElementById('shell');
  var box=document.getElementById('ht-toggle');
  if(!shell||!box) return;
  window.HT=function(){ return shell.classList.contains('hide-text'); };
  function apply(){
    shell.classList.toggle('hide-text', box.checked);
    window.dispatchEvent(new Event('resize')); /* forces a redraw in every CM sim, even while paused */
  }
  box.addEventListener('change', apply);
  /* Default: follow lecture mode at boot. Must wait for window load — in these ~300KB
     files a rAF can fire mid-parse, BEFORE the end-of-body auto-lecture script has run
     (verified live in L4). Independent thereafter. */
  window.addEventListener('load', function(){
    requestAnimationFrame(function(){ requestAnimationFrame(function(){
      box.checked = shell.classList.contains('lecture-mode');
      apply();
    });});
  });
})();
</script>
```

## Registering items later (NOT part of installation)

Installation ships the container **empty**. When asked to register text:
- **DOM items** (panels, HTML legends, readouts): add `ht-hide` to the **complete visible
  element**, not just its text node — a legend entry includes its colour swatch/icon; a
  chip includes its pill background. Hiding only the text and leaving an orphaned dot in
  an empty pill is wrong (this exact failure occurred in L4).
  **No orphaned chrome:** if hiding leaves a container with no visible children (e.g. a
  legend chip whose other entries are `display:none`), register the container itself.
- **Canvas text** (`fillText`/label helpers): wrap the call site in `if(!HT()){ … }`.
  On canvas, never gate physics content — arrows, markers, trajectories, geometry —
  text labels only, unless explicitly asked. (The protection is for *physics* drawings;
  DOM UI chrome accompanying text is part of the item and gets hidden with it.)
- Append a one-line entry to the `HIDE-TEXT REGISTRY` comment for every item, replacing
  the `(empty — …)` line on first registration.

## Rules

- **Install must not hide anything.** The registry starts empty; the checkbox visibly
  toggling class `hide-text` with zero visual change is the *correct* install state.
- **Never delete text** through this mechanism — hide-only, reversible by design.
- **Idempotent:** if `id="ht-toggle"` already exists in the file, skip it entirely.
- **Scope:** `Capacity_CM_simulations/*.html` **excluding** `index.html`, `vendor/`,
  and anything under `CM_lecture_sims_backup/`.
- Do not touch physics code, the shell loop, or the auto-lecture script.

## Verify after installing (per sim)

1. `id="ht-toggle"` appears exactly once; registry comment appears exactly once.
2. Load the sim: checkbox renders beside 🎓 Lecture, zero console errors. Boot default
   differs by family: **CM** sims boot into lecture mode → checkbox CHECKED at load;
   **particle-physics** sims boot into guided inquiry → the load-sync is inert and the
   checkbox is UNCHECKED at load (correct — text visible by default; Hide Text stays
   independent of the 🎓 Lecture toggle unless explicitly coupled later).
3. Toggling it adds/removes `hide-text` on `#shell` and nothing visible changes (empty registry).
4. Physics untouched: no edits inside the sim's main IIFE.
